From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: drm: only force the DV tunnel wire format when the output is DV

meson_hdmitx_decide_color_attr forces the Dolby Vision tunnelling wire
format (RGB/444 8-bit for STD, YUV422 12-bit for LL) whenever the amdv
core is enabled. That predicate is too broad: VS10 can run the DV core
(FEL expand, DM tone-map) while the OUTPUT is forced to HDR10 or SDR
(dolby_vision_mode HDR10/SDR10/SDR8).

Sequence on a VS10 DV->HDR10 playback: amdv engages HDR10 and hdmitx
accepts the DRM packet on the existing 10/12-bit wire (the HDR10 toast
the user briefly sees). ~1s later Kodi's refresh-rate switch triggers a
DRM modeset; decide_color_attr sees is_amdv_enable() and forces the wire
to YUV444 8-bit. The modeset teardown drops the DRM packet ("Dolby VSIF,
switching signal to SDR") and the new 8-bit wire makes
hdmitx_set_drm_pkt refuse every subsequent HDR10 packet (8-bit +
!config_csc_en -> forced BT709 SDR), so the signal latches on 8-bit SDR
for the rest of playback. Same mechanism for DV FEL and profile 8.1 on
every SoC family (hdmitx20 and hdmitx21).

Gate the two format-force sites on the amdv TARGET OUTPUT mode instead:
keep the tunnel force for IPT/IPT_TUNNEL (and BYPASS, matching today's
behaviour while the mode is not yet resolved), skip it when VS10 targets
HDR10/SDR10/SDR8 so the native attr/EDID selection (e.g. 422,12bit)
carries the forced-HDR10 signal exactly like native HDR10 playback.

--- a/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
@@ -286,6 +286,23 @@
 		return true;
 }
 
+/* The Dolby Vision tunnelling wire-format constraints (RGB/444 8-bit for
+ * STD, YUV422 12-bit for LL) only apply when the signal on the wire is
+ * actually Dolby Vision. VS10 can run the DV core while outputting
+ * HDR10/SDR (forced output mode); those cases must keep the native
+ * format selection: an 8-bit wire makes hdmitx refuse the HDR10 DRM
+ * packet and drop the signal to SDR.
+ */
+static bool is_amdv_output_dv(void)
+{
+	int mode = get_amdv_target_mode();
+
+	return is_amdv_enable() &&
+	       mode != AMDV_OUTPUT_MODE_HDR10 &&
+	       mode != AMDV_OUTPUT_MODE_SDR10 &&
+	       mode != AMDV_OUTPUT_MODE_SDR8;
+}
+
 static int meson_hdmitx_decide_color_attr
 	(struct hdmitx_common *common, struct am_meson_crtc_state *crtc_state,
 	struct hdmitx_color_attr *attr, u64 sequence_id)
@@ -319,7 +336,7 @@
 	// try autoselect
 	// check if any colour subsampling is set
 	// force colour subsampling when DV mode
-	if (is_amdv_enable()) {
+	if (is_amdv_output_dv()) {
 		int cs = attr->colorformat;
 		if (get_amdv_ll_policy() == 0 /* DOLBY_VISION_LL_DISABLE */) {
 			attr->colorformat = HDMI_COLORSPACE_YUV444;
@@ -362,7 +379,7 @@
 
 	// check for bit colourdepth limit
 	// force bit colourdepth when DV mode
-	if (is_amdv_enable()) {
+	if (is_amdv_output_dv()) {
 		int cd = bitdepth_to_colordepth(attr->bitdepth);
 		if (get_amdv_ll_policy() == 0 /* DOLBY_VISION_LL_DISABLE */) {
 			attr->bitdepth = colordepth_to_bitdepth(COLORDEPTH_24B);
